||imasdk.googleapis.com^
||doubleclick.net^
||conviva.com^
||browser-intake-datadoghq.com^
||eligibility-panelresearch.googlevideo.com^

! ---- Background telemetry from preinstalled Netflix / Prime Video apps ----
||ichnaea.netflix.com^
||customerevents.netflix.com^
||telemetry.insights.video.a2z.com^
||minerva.devices.a2z.com^
! Prime Video client telemetry: the TV's biggest non-video uploader (961K in 9 conns, 2026-10-25)
||unagi-na.amazon.com^

! ---- Added from the 2026-10-25 eth0 capture ----
! LG Channels promo thumbnails, fetched over plain HTTP
||itsmy.tv^
! ---- ThinQ / IoT / cloud push (user does not use ThinQ; decided 2026-10-25) ----
! lgtviot.com + lgthinq.com are LG's IoT/ThinQ backends; the AWS IoT host is the MQTT push
! channel the TV opened tonight. Unblock all three if you ever want the ThinQ app to control the TV.
||lgtviot.com^
||lgthinq.com^
||a16i6ajbm83mvw-ats.iot.us-west-2.amazonaws.com^

! ---- Voice / speech back-ends (decided 2026-10-26) ----
! The CX has no built-in microphone; the Magic Remote mic is push-to-talk and the TV refuses
! voice recognition while the "Voice Information" agreement is declined (verified: a button press
! produced a consent prompt and zero network activity). These make that a wall, not a checkbox.
! netflixvoice.lgtvcommon.com and lgthinq.com (LG's own speech/AI) are blocked above.
! Not googleapis.com wholesale: YouTube needs www. and youtubei.googleapis.com.
||embeddedassistant.googleapis.com^
||avs-alexa-na.amazon.com^
||avs-alexa-eu.amazon.com^
||avs-alexa-fe.amazon.com^
||api.amazonalexa.com^
||dangbei.com^

! ---- Home-screen declutter (promo rows / thumbnails; decided 2026-10-25) ----
! Fewer rows for the 2020 SoC to render. Unblock a host if thumbnails break inside an app you use.
! NOT us.lgrecommends.lgappstv.com: the Content Store's landing page is that feed and the store
! app fails outright without it (found 2026-10-26).
||img.nvidiagrid.net^
||images.pluto.tv^
||canvas.tubitv.com^
||images.redbox.com^
||cdn77.utomik.com^
||blacknut-prod-images-cdn.b-cdn.net^
! Audience measurement + app telemetry seen from the Peacock app
||omtrdc.net^
||imrworldwide.com^
||scorecardresearch.com^
||nr-data.net^
! Amazon ad tracking pixel (s.amazon-adsystem.com during Prime Video ads)
||amazon-adsystem.com^
! Peacock's first-party telemetry ingest (86K uploaded in a 45-min session). Verified
! 2026-10-25: playback, CDN switching, token refresh and pause/resume all fine with it blocked.
||ingest.webcol.sdp.peacocktv.com^
! Tried and rejected 2026-10-25: ||aiv-delivery.net^ (Prime Video's ad-pod service, ters-sgai1 /
! ters-draper1). Ads still played with it blocked: the ad video is stitched into the stream
! from the same CDNs as the show, so DNS cannot remove Prime ads. Don't bother again.

! ---- Audience measurement seen during a day of YouTube (2026-10-26) ----
! Google's TV "user panel" API and the per-device panel-research host (YouTube viewing measurement);
! HaGeZi Pro already covers googlesyndication/doubleclick, this fills the gaps it leaves.
||userpaneltv-pa.googleapis.com^
/-panelresearch\.googlevideo\.com$/
! Neustar ad-data pixel (d.agkn.com) fired by the Peacock app's ad stack
||agkn.com^
! Chrome update/usage pings from the TV's browser engine; no function on a TV
||tools.google.com^
! WebRTC STUN discovery from the browser engine
||stun.services.mozilla.com^

! ---- From the 2026-10-26 community research: newer webOS generations (unverified on this CX) ----
! Pure ad/telemetry hosts captured on webOS 24/25 sets (HaGeZi #11412/#11438, webosbrew apps-repo #254,
! Level1Techs), no breakage reported. The CX never contacts them; kept so the profile is right for
! a newer LG. The aws-prd.net rules are regexes on the CNAME targets, never the zone: must-allow
! hosts (us.lgtvsdp.com, lgtvonline.lge.com, the store feed/API) CNAME into aws-prd.net as well.
/^[a-z]{2}-(ad|info)-lgsmartad-com\.aws-prd\.net$/
/^[a-z]{2}-rdx2-lgtvsdp-com\.aws-prd\.net$/
||videoads.lgtvcommon.com^
||adts.lgtvcommon.com^
! Samba TV ran ACR on non-US LG sets until 2022-09 (libsambasolution.so); Nielsen's library ships too
||samba.tv^
||nielsentam.tv^
! ad SSP seen on webOS 25 (mitm) and 24; public-IP lookup before the first video frame
||adstk.io^
||api.ipify.org^
! LG Shop promos (sdx service map, medium confidence)
||lgshopsvc.lgappstv.com^
